    "q-140852": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140852",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+(-6)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =3-12+20 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
