    "q-93967": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93967",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot (-4)+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-8+12+2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
