    "q-93969": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93969",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-6-4+3 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
