      "dom_id": "step-q93980",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
