    "q-93917": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93917",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4+4-3-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-93917-a",
