      "knowledge_point": "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix",
      "kp_id": "e-8162"
    },
    "q-94040": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94040",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$",
      "worked_solution": "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1$ and $b=2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+2=3.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
