    "q-94048": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94048",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & b \\\\ a & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a-b?$",
      "worked_solution": "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,\\,+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=b=2.$ Finally,\n\n$$\na-b=2-2=0.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
