      "dom_id": "step-q94042",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 2 \\\\ b & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$",
      "worked_solution": "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,4{x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,+1{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1$ and $b=4.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+4=5.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
